.TH CONDUCTOR-BACKUP 8 "2026-10-03" "Samba Conductor" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
conductor-backup \- encrypted Samba AD backups, restore and restore drills
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conductor-backup
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conductor-backup
takes online backups of a Samba Active Directory domain through
.BR conductor-helper (8),
encrypts them with age to recipients whose private keys are kept off the
domain controller, uploads them with signed manifests, prunes by a retention
policy and alerts on failures. On a separate drill host it restores the
newest backup into a sandbox without network and checks it. The default
configuration is
.IR /etc/conductor-backup/conductor-backup.toml .
.SH COMMANDS
On a domain controller (user conductor-backup):
.TP
.B run [\-\-scheduled|\-\-now]
Back up when due (timer) or now, upload, verify, prune, exchange drill
requests and reports, alert.
.TP
.B request backup|drill [\-\-wait]
Ask the service for a backup or a drill now.
.TP
.B check
Evaluate and send alerts only (exit 1 if any is active).
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Status as shown on conductor's Backups page.
.TP
.B list [\-\-destination N]
Backups in a destination (signatures verified).
.TP
.B verify ID|latest
Download and check the SHA-256 (no decryption).
.TP
.B prune [\-\-dry\-run]
Apply the retention policy.
.PP
Anywhere with read access to the bucket (root, with the offline key):
.TP
.B restore ID|latest \-\-identity FILE \-\-target DIR \-\-newservername NAME
Restore a backup with samba-tool domain backup restore.
.PP
On a drill host (root, never a domain controller):
.TP
.B drill [\-\-now] [\-\-backup ID]
Run a requested (or forced) restore drill.
.PP
Keys:
.TP
.B keygen signing|age \-\-out FILE
Create a signing key or an age identity.
.TP
.BI pubkey " FILE"
Public key of a signing key.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-backup/conductor-backup.toml
Configuration on a domain controller.
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-backup/drill.toml
Configuration on a drill host.
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-backup/recipients.txt
age recipients (root-owned, writable by root only).
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-backup/credentials/
Signing key, S3 and SMTP credentials, backup account password, drill
identity, loaded by systemd.
.TP
.I /usr/share/conductor-backup/systemd/conductor-helper-backup.conf
Drop-in for conductor-helper.service, linked when backups are enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conductor (8),
.BR conductor-helper (8),
.BR age (1)
